I am testing open:creib.forge.conformance.oracle.recover_json_object. Its documented rule says: "The object scored is the last one inside a code fence when any fence holds one, else the last top-level object in the text, because a model places its final answer last and marks it: a reply that quotes its previous answer and then gives a corrected one is scored on the correction." Reply one is '```json\n{"p":1}\n{"q":2}\n```\n{"r":3}'. Reply two is '```json\n{"p":1}\n{"q":5}\n```\n{"r":3}'. The rule requires reply one to be scored as {"q":2} and reply two as {"q":5}, because each has a code fence holding two top-level objects and the last one inside the fence is the final answer. I would be wrong if recover_json_object returns {"q":2} for reply one and {"q":5} for reply two, or if it returns any two different answers for the two replies.